    "notes": "Custom Ava Zero evaluation through the avartha_pipecat adapter against a hosted Ava Zero agent on the Avartha Platform over WebRTC. The agent uses GLM-5.3 as its frontend, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 at max reasoning as its backend worker, and Qwen3-ASR-1.7B for speech recognition. Agent build 1138c346, whose English behaviour is identical to b680a988 in our standard v1.1 entry. The voice user simulator's customer LLM is gpt-5.5-2026-04-23 at xhigh reasoning effort; the other simulator components, benchmark prompts, policies, tools and evaluator are unchanged, and this non-default customer LLM makes the result a custom submission. Harness: tau2 2.0.0 (main at c06b07d) with an earlier revision of the #758 avartha_pipecat adapter: as at 6e563dd, without that commit's tolerance for a resampler-delayed lost-media stamp and without the quiet-tail fixes added after it. Regular speech complexity, seed 300, 0.2-second ticks, 2400-second call limit, the default hallucination reviewer, and no reward or agent-error reruns. One trial was scheduled for every base task (airline 50, retail 114, telecom 114), 30 calls at a time; calls that hit an infrastructure error were re-run from the start (4 in this run). The English caller personas used our own voices (TAU2_VOICE_ID_EN_*), not Sierra-managed voices.",
